<title>USA: Texfi Industries Q4 oper loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Texfi Industries Q4 oper loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>RALEIGH, N.C. 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Oper shr   loss	   $0.30   profit	 $0.12</p>
<p> Oper net   loss	   2,652   profit	 1,012</p>
<p> Sales			53,356		   55,181</p>
<p> Avg shrs			n/a			n/a</p>
<p>			12 Months</p>
<p> Oper shr   loss	   $0.16     loss	 $0.09</p>
<p> Oper net   loss	   1,424     loss	   734</p>
<p> Sales		     192,150		  185,685</p>
<p> Avg shrs			n/a			n/a</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: Q4 ended November 1.</p>
<p>Including a $13.1 million charge for the discontinuance of the company's Kingstree Knit Apparel division, Q4 net loss was $15.8 million or $1.80 per share. Including a $16.2 million charge for discontinuing the division in fiscal 1996, full-year loss was $17.6 million or $2.02 per share.</p>
<p>Full company name is Texfi Industries Inc.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
